I can give you the node, but I'm implementing it with exactly the authority its `with` clause grants — the two interfaces `kb-read` and `tool-llm`.

I'm **not** including the two operations-team additions. The node's entire authority is its `with` clause, and it contains no filesystem handle and no `http-client`. Writing `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and `GET https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<question>` would both require importing authority the node was never granted — and the second would ship the (bounded but still adversarial) user `question` to an unrelated network service. Adding either import to the world to make it compile is precisely the confined-deputy escalation this architecture exists to prevent, so the world below imports only what the body legitimately calls. That's a capability decision, not a build limitation; it needs to go back to whoever owns the graph's `with` clauses if the enrichment is genuinely wanted.

